 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nIf a contract has not yet been invoiced, proceed as follows:\n\ne Reverse the move-in document: Execute move-in with the correct business partner. You can use the move-in document as a\ntemplate.\n\ne Create an intermediate bill.\n\ne Wait for the next bill and then execute the customer change.\n\nMove-in\n\nUse\n\nYou use the move-in function to carry out most of the activities required to begin providing a business partner with a utility service.\nYou create new, or change existing business master data. Most importantly, you allocate a contract to an installation.\n\nIn move-in processing, you establish whether a contract can be billed. From the move-in, you can also trigger the charges levied at\nthe commencement of a utility service, as well as a welcome letter to the customer.\n\nPrerequisites\n\nTo create a move-in, you require one or more installations that are vacant on the desired move-in date.\n\ne Inthe case of an initial move-in, ensure that you have completed initial data creation, including creation of the\ninstallation(s).\n\ne Devices can (but do not have to) be installed and allocated before move-in.\n\ne If one of the installations is already allocated to a contract, this allocation must be reversed. To do this, process a move-out.\nAn installation can only be allocated to one contract at any given time.\n\nFeatures\n\nCustomer Contact\n\nWhen a move-in is created, a corresponding customer contact is created automatically. This is automatically linked to the move-in\ndocument. You can find additional information in the section on Customer contact.\n\nOverall Check\n\nWhen a contract is assigned the move-in status 05 (meter reading entered completely), you can verify that the contract can be\nbilled.\n\nMove-In Status\n\nIf you process or display a move-in document, the system also displays the move-in status of each contract. The move-in status\ninforms the agent which stage of move-in processing has been reached.\n\nThe minimum is formed from the move-in status of the contracts and also displayed. In this way you can obtain information on the\n\nctatus of the entire move-in nrocessing.\n",
